  ],
  "lines": {
    "n01": "AI agents are already part of how companies work.",
    "n02": "People ask them to read files, answer customers, write code, and move money.",
    "n04": "But a language model is non-deterministic.",
    "n05": "Ask it the same thing twice, and the reasoning, the plan, even the action can change.",
    "n06": "That's fine for a first draft. It's not fine for permissions.",
    "n07": "So who decides what an agent may actually do? The model, or the company?",
    "n08": "Betsee. Better see what your agents do, and deterministically control what they can do.",
    "n09": "Your people keep the assistants they already love: Claude Code or Codex, running inside Betsee Desk.",
    "n10": "Every message is checked before the model ever sees it: card numbers, IBANs, keys, and restricted names never leave.",
    "n11": "And every tool call goes to the Betsee Gateway first. If the Gateway can't be reached, nothing runs.",
    "n12": "The Gateway decides every action in fifteen deterministic stages.",
    "n13": "Identity, context, capability, Cedar policy, information tier, command validation, and budget.",
    "n14": "AI analysis comes after policy, and it can only make a decision stricter.",
    "n15": "Then approval, step-up, execution, and audit. Every stage is a span. Every decision is a trace.",
    "n16": "Same conditions. Same policy. Same decision.",
    "n17": "Run it again and again, and the answer never changes. Change one real condition, and the decision changes, predictably.",
    "n18": "AI may tighten a decision.",
    "n18b": "It can never silently loosen your boundary.",
    "n19": "The Director shows your entire AI organization, live.",
    "n20": "What needs attention right now.",
    "n20b": "Every decision as it happens.",
    "n20c": "Who touched what.",
    "n21": "And for every agent, the exact permissions it holds: delegated by a person, intersected with policy.",
    "n22": "Open any decision and follow it all the way down: who asked, through which agent, for what, on which resource, and the exact rule that decided it.",
    "n23": "High-impact actions wait for a human. The approver sees the exact action and the parameters the Gateway recorded.",
    "n24": "They prove who they are with a fresh one-time code. The approval becomes part of the context, and the same policy decides again.",
    "n25": "In Policy Studio, business intent sits on top. Underneath, Cedar policies enforce it, before anything executes.",
    "n26": "Sensitive data stays inside its boundary. A changed tool is blocked before any agent sees it.",
    "n27": "A runaway agent hits its budget and is quarantined. And one agent can't borrow another agent's permissions.",
    "n28": "Every control maps to a risk. And every decision leaves evidence.",
    "n29": "Models will change. Agents will change. Your enterprise boundary remains yours.",
    "n30": "Use AI, without handing control to AI.",
    "n31": "Betsee. Non-deterministic AI. Deterministic control."
  }
}
